course: dictionary
lesson: 14111
title: Words from the body
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Metabolise is a verb, so it describes something that happens or something you do. Look at the words around it for clues. «Your body metabolises the bread you eat, so it can give you energy and help you grow.» Eating, energy and growing all point to a process that uses food.
explain: The same word also works for medicine. «The doctor said Sam's body metabolises the medicine in a few hours.» Here the body is changing the medicine, so metabolise means to process and change it.
explain: A good check is to swap in a simpler phrase. Try «breaks down and uses» in the first sentence: «Your body breaks down and uses the bread you eat.» It still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: Metabolise is a verb: metabolise, metabolises, metabolised, metabolising.
fact: To metabolise food means the body breaks it down and uses it for energy and growth.
fact: To metabolise a medicine or substance means the body processes it and changes it.
fact: «Metabolise» is linked to metabolism, the body's chemical processes that keep you alive.
fact: British English spells it metabolise; American English writes metabolize, with the same meaning.
exercise: «Your body metabolises the apple you ate at break.» What does metabolise mean here? | To store food in a fridge | To throw food away | To cook food in an oven | *To break food down and use it for energy and growth
exercise: «The doctor said Sam's body metabolises the medicine within a few hours.» What is the body doing to the medicine? | *To process and change it | To make it into a sweet drink | To hide it from the blood | To freeze it solid
exercise: «Mia metabolised her lunch quickly.» Find and copy the word that is a form of metabolise. | quickly | lunch | *metabolised | Mia
test: «Food gives us energy only after our bodies have metabolised it.» What has to happen before food gives us energy? | It must be left in the sun | It must be thrown away | It must be frozen | *It must be broken down by the body
test: «Ben's body metabolises his medicine slowly.» Which word is closest in meaning to metabolises? | Ignores | Smells | *Processes | Cools
exam: Lily says metabolise means to eat very fast. What does it really mean? | *The body breaks down and uses food or medicine | To eat very fast | To sleep deeply at night | To drink lots of water
